/-!
# Criteria for a morphism to have constant relative dimension

Let `f : X ⟶ S` be locally of finite type and let `F` be a quasi-coherent `𝒪_X`-module of finite
type whose support is all of `X`. If `F` is flat over `S` in codimension `0`, that is at every
generic point of every fibre, then the dimension of a fibre component generated by a
specialization of a point `ξ` which is generic in its own fibre does not depend on the component
or on the fibre. This file derives from that the two criteria of Tag 0GSK for `f` to have
relative dimension `d` in the sense of Tag 02NJ: that `X` be irreducible with generic point `ξ`
whose residue field has transcendence degree `d` over `κ(f ξ)`, and that some fibre be dense in
`X` with all its irreducible components of dimension `d`.

## Main results

* `Stacks.RelativeAssassin.topologicalKrullDim_component_fiber_eq_of_specializes`: any two
  components of fibres, each generated by a specialization of `ξ`, have the same dimension.
* `Stacks.RelativeAssassin.relativeDimension_of_isGenericPoint_of_trdeg`: the first criterion of
  Tag 0GSK.
* `Stacks.RelativeAssassin.relativeDimension_of_dense_fiber_of_component_dim`: the second
  criterion of Tag 0GSK.

## Implementation notes

The source states Tag 0GSK without proof, deferring it; the derivation here is the one its text
indicates, through Tag 0GSJ, and in fact through the fibre dimension equality of Tag 0GSI that
Tag 0GSJ rests on, which is what applies to a single component of a single fibre.

Given a point `ξ`, write `Y` for the reduced closed subscheme supported on the closure of `ξ` and
`g` for the induced morphism `Y ⟶ S`. The engine is applied along the closed embedding
`Stacks.RelativeAssassin.closureFiberIncl` of the fibre `Y_s` into the fibre `X_s`, whose range
is the part of `X_s` lying in the closure of `ξ`. A component of `X_s` whose generic point
specializes from `ξ` is contained in that range, and corresponds there to a component of `Y_s`
of the same dimension; Tag 0GSI evaluates the local dimension of `Y_s` at the generic point of
that component as the dimension of `Y_{f ξ}`, a quantity not depending on `s`. Applying this
twice, once at the given fibre and once at the fibre of `ξ` itself, eliminates `Y` from the
statement.

That `ξ` lies in the relative assassin `Ass_{X/S}(F)`, which Tag 0GSI requires, is not an extra
hypothesis: a fibre of a morphism locally of finite type is locally Noetherian, so a point of
the support of a module on it which is minimal in that support is an associated point, and the
support of the restriction of `F` to a fibre is the whole fibre because the support of `F` is all
of `X`.

The flatness hypothesis is the weakened one that the source's last sentence allows, flatness over
`S` at every generic point of every fibre; flatness over `S` everywhere, which is what the
source's lists ask for, implies it by `fun s z _ => hF _`. Transcendence degree is a `Cardinal`
while dimensions take values in `WithBot ℕ∞`, so the hypothesis on it is stated through
`Cardinal.toENat`, as in the fibre dimension formula
`AlgebraicGeometry.topologicalKrullDimAt_fiber_eq_ringKrullDim_stalk_add_trdeg`.

For the second criterion the density hypothesis is turned into the specialization the engine
wants: above an affine open `U` of `X` the fibre `X_η` is affine, because the fibre inclusion is
an affine morphism, hence a Noetherian space, hence covered by the closures of the generic points
of its finitely many irreducible components; the union of the closures in `X` of those finitely
many points is therefore closed and contains `X_η ∩ U`, so it contains `U` by density. A generic
point of a component of `X_η ∩ U` is a generic point of a component of `X_η`, since the closure
of the component it generates is the irreducible component of `X_η` through it.

## Coverage limits

Both sets of hypotheses are formalized, with two deliberate departures from the source, recorded
in the docstrings of the two theorems. In both, the flatness of `F` over `S` is weakened to
flatness in codimension `0`, which is what the proof uses and what the source's last sentence
announces. In the second, the source's first hypothesis, that `S` be irreducible with `η` its
generic point, is dropped: what the argument uses is the density of the fibre over the chosen
point `η`, which is the source's second hypothesis, so `η` is an arbitrary point of `S` here and
the source's statement is the case of the generic point of an irreducible `S`. The integrality of
`X` in the first set is kept as the source states it, although only the irreducibility is
used.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0GSK](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0GSK)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0GSJ](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0GSJ)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0GSI](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0GSI)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 02NJ](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/02NJ)
-/

@[expose] public section

open AlgebraicGeometry CategoryTheory TopologicalSpace

universe u

namespace Stacks.RelativeAssassin

variable {X S : Scheme.{u}}

private instance locallyOfFiniteType_fiberToSpecResidueField (f : X ⟶ S)
    [LocallyOfFiniteType f] (s : S) : LocallyOfFiniteType (f.fiberToSpecResidueField s) := by
  change LocallyOfFiniteType (Limits.pullback.snd f (S.fromSpecResidueField s))
  infer_instance

private instance isLocallyNoetherian_fiber (f : X ⟶ S) [LocallyOfFiniteType f] (s : S) :
    IsLocallyNoetherian (f.fiber s) :=
  LocallyOfFiniteType.isLocallyNoetherian (f.fiberToSpecResidueField s)

/-- The point of a fibre determined by a generic point of the source is a generic point of that
fibre. -/
private theorem isGenericPoint_asFiber (f : X ⟶ S) (t : X)
    (ht : IsGenericPoint t (Set.univ : Set X)) :
    IsGenericPoint (f.asFiber t) (Set.univ : Set (f.fiber (f t))) := by
  refine isGenericPoint_def.mpr (Set.eq_univ_iff_forall.mpr fun z =>
    specializes_iff_mem_closure.mp ?_)
  apply (f.fiberι (f t)).isEmbedding.isInducing.specializes_iff.mp
  rw [f.fiberι_asFiber t]
  exact ht.specializes (Set.mem_univ _)

/-- A point generating an irreducible component is a generic point of the space. -/
private theorem mem_genericPoints_of_isGenericPoint {T : Type*} [TopologicalSpace T] {t : T}
    {C : Set T} (hC : C ∈ irreducibleComponents T) (htC : IsGenericPoint t C) :
    t ∈ genericPoints T := by
  change closure ({t} : Set T) ∈ irreducibleComponents T
  rwa [htC.def]

/-- The inclusion of the fibre of a closed subscheme into the fibre of the ambient scheme. -/
private noncomputable def closureFiberIncl (f : X ⟶ S) (Y : X.IdealSheafData) (s : S) :
    (Y.subschemeι ≫ f).fiber s → f.fiber s := fun a =>
  (f.fiberHomeo s).symm ⟨Y.subschemeι ((Y.subschemeι ≫ f).fiberι s a), by
    simpa only [Set.mem_preimage, Set.mem_singleton_iff, Scheme.Hom.comp_apply] using
      (Y.subschemeι ≫ f).apply_fiberι s a⟩

/-- The inclusion of fibres is compatible with the two fibre embeddings. -/
private theorem fiberι_closureFiberIncl (f : X ⟶ S) (Y : X.IdealSheafData) (s : S)
    (a : (Y.subschemeι ≫ f).fiber s) :
    f.fiberι s (closureFiberIncl f Y s a) =
      Y.subschemeι ((Y.subschemeι ≫ f).fiberι s a) :=
  f.fiberι_fiberHomeo_symm s _

/-- The inclusion of fibres is continuous. -/
private theorem continuous_closureFiberIncl (f : X ⟶ S) (Y : X.IdealSheafData) (s : S) :
    Continuous (closureFiberIncl f Y s) := by
  apply (f.fiberHomeo s).symm.continuous.comp
  apply Continuous.subtype_mk
  exact Y.subschemeι.continuous.comp ((Y.subschemeι ≫ f).fiberι s).continuous

/-- The range of the inclusion of fibres is the part of the fibre lying in the subscheme. -/
private theorem range_closureFiberIncl (f : X ⟶ S) (Y : X.IdealSheafData) (s : S) :
    Set.range (closureFiberIncl f Y s) = f.fiberι s ⁻¹' (Y.support : Set X) := by
  ext b
  rw [Set.mem_preimage, ← Y.range_subschemeι]
  constructor
  · rintro ⟨a, rfl⟩
    exact ⟨_, (fiberι_closureFiberIncl f Y s a).symm⟩
  · rintro ⟨y, hy⟩
    have hgy : (Y.subschemeι ≫ f) y = s := by
      rw [Scheme.Hom.comp_apply, hy, f.apply_fiberι]
    refine ⟨((Y.subschemeι ≫ f).fiberHomeo s).symm ⟨y, hgy⟩, ?_⟩
    apply (f.fiberι s).isEmbedding.injective
    rwa [fiberι_closureFiberIncl, (Y.subschemeι ≫ f).fiberι_fiberHomeo_symm s ⟨y, hgy⟩]

/-- The inclusion of fibres is a closed embedding. -/
private theorem isClosedEmbedding_closureFiberIncl (f : X ⟶ S) (Y : X.IdealSheafData) (s : S) :
    Topology.IsClosedEmbedding (closureFiberIncl f Y s) := by
  constructor
  · refine Topology.IsEmbedding.of_comp (continuous_closureFiberIncl f Y s)
      (f.fiberι s).continuous ?_
    rw [show (f.fiberι s) ∘ (closureFiberIncl f Y s) =
        Y.subschemeι ∘ ((Y.subschemeι ≫ f).fiberι s) from funext (fiberι_closureFiberIncl f Y s)]
    exact Y.subschemeι.isEmbedding.comp ((Y.subschemeι ≫ f).fiberι s).isEmbedding
  · rw [range_closureFiberIncl]
    exact Y.support.isClosed.preimage (f.fiberι s).continuous

/-- A generic point of a fibre at which the module does not vanish lies in the relative
assassin. The fibre is locally Noetherian, the point is minimal in the support of the
restriction of the module to that fibre, and a minimal point of the support is an associated
point. -/
private theorem mem_relativeAssassin_of_mem_genericPoints_fiber (f : X ⟶ S)
    [LocallyOfFiniteType f] (F : X.Modules) [F.IsQuasicoherent] [F.IsFiniteType]
    (hsupp : SheafOfModules.supp F = Set.univ)
    (ξ : X) (hξ : f.asFiber ξ ∈ genericPoints (f.fiber (f ξ))) :
    ξ ∈ Stacks.Divisors.relativeAssassin f F := by
  let Fξ := (Scheme.Modules.pullback (f.fiberι (f ξ))).obj F
  have : Fξ.IsFiniteType :=
    AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.pullback_isFiniteType
      (f.fiberι (f ξ)).toLRSHom.toShHom F
  have : Fξ.IsQuasicoherent :=
    Stacks.Modules.isQuasicoherent_pullback (f.fiberι (f ξ)) F inferInstance
  have hmem : f.asFiber ξ ∈ SheafOfModules.supp Fξ := by
    rw [Stacks.Modules.supp_pullback, hsupp, Set.preimage_univ]
    trivial
  have hrel := (Stacks.Divisors.mem_associatedPoints_fiber_iff_mem_relativeAssassin f F (f ξ)
    (f.asFiber ξ)).mp (AlgebraicGeometry.mem_associatedPoints_of_mem_supp_of_specialization
      (f.fiber (f ξ)) Fξ (f.asFiber ξ) hmem fun y _ hy =>
        (mem_genericPoints_iff_forall_specializes_eq (f.asFiber ξ)).1 hξ y hy)
  rwa [f.fiberι_asFiber ξ] at hrel

/-- A morphism all of whose fibre components have dimension `d` has relative dimension `d`. -/
theorem relativeDimension_of_forall_component (f : X ⟶ S) [LocallyOfFiniteType f]
    (d : ℕ) (hdim : ∀ (s : S) (C : Set (f.fiber s)), C ∈ irreducibleComponents (f.fiber s) →
      topologicalKrullDim C = (d : WithBot ℕ∞)) :
    AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeDimension f d := by
  intro s hne
  refine ⟨fun Z hZ W hW => by rw [hdim s Z hZ, hdim s W hW], ?_⟩
  have hlocal : ∀ z : f.fiber s, topologicalKrullDimAt (f.fiber s) z = (d : WithBot ℕ∞) := by
    intro z
    obtain ⟨Z, hZ, -, hZd⟩ :=
      exists_mem_irreducibleComponents_topologicalKrullDim_eq_topologicalKrullDimAt
        (S.residueField s) (f.fiber s) (f.fiberToSpecResidueField s) z
    exact hZd.symm.trans (hdim s Z hZ)
  obtain ⟨z⟩ := hne
  rw [TopologicalSpace.topologicalKrullDim_eq_iSup_localKrullDim]
  simp_rw [← TopologicalSpace.topologicalKrullDimAt_eq_localKrullDim, hlocal]
  exact le_antisymm (iSup_le fun _ => le_rfl) (le_iSup_of_le z le_rfl)

/-- A subset whose image under a continuous injection is an irreducible component, and which is
itself irreducible, is an irreducible component. -/
theorem mem_irreducibleComponents_of_image {A B : Type*} [TopologicalSpace A]
    [TopologicalSpace B] {ρ : A → B} (hρc : Continuous ρ) (hρi : Function.Injective ρ)
    {Z : Set A} (hZ : IsIrreducible Z) (hC : ρ '' Z ∈ irreducibleComponents B) :
    Z ∈ irreducibleComponents A := by
  refine ⟨hZ, fun W hW hsub w hw => ?_⟩
  obtain ⟨v, hv, hvw⟩ := hC.2 (hW.image _ hρc.continuousOn) (Set.image_mono hsub) ⟨w, hw, rfl⟩
  rwa [← hρi hvw]

/-- The dimension of a component of a fibre through a specialization of a relative associated
point `ξ`, in terms of the reduced closure `Y` of `ξ`: it is the dimension of the fibre of `Y`
over the image of `ξ`. -/
private theorem topologicalKrullDim_component_fiber_eq_closureFiber (f : X ⟶ S)
    [LocallyOfFiniteType f] (F : X.Modules) [F.IsQuasicoherent] [F.IsFiniteType]
    (ξ : X) (hξ : ξ ∈ Stacks.Divisors.relativeAssassin f F)
    (s : S) (x : f.fiber s) (hx : ξ ⤳ f.fiberι s x)
    (C : Set (f.fiber s)) (hC : C ∈ irreducibleComponents (f.fiber s))
    (hxC : IsGenericPoint x C)
    (hflat : AlgebraicGeometry.IsFlatOverAt f.toLRSHom.toShHom F (f.fiberι s x)) :
    topologicalKrullDim C = topologicalKrullDim
      (((Scheme.IdealSheafData.vanishingIdeal
        (Closeds.closure ({ξ} : Set X))).subschemeι ≫ f).fiber (f ξ)) := by
  let Y := Scheme.IdealSheafData.vanishingIdeal (Closeds.closure ({ξ} : Set X))
  let g : Y.subscheme ⟶ S := Y.subschemeι ≫ f
  have : LocallyOfFiniteType g := by
    dsimp only [g]
    infer_instance
  obtain ⟨x', hρx⟩ : x ∈ Set.range (closureFiberIncl f Y s) := by
    rw [range_closureFiberIncl, Set.mem_preimage,
      Scheme.IdealSheafData.coe_support_vanishingIdeal]
    exact specializes_iff_mem_closure.mp hx
  have hclρ : Topology.IsClosedEmbedding (closureFiberIncl f Y s) :=
    isClosedEmbedding_closureFiberIncl f Y s
  have himg : closureFiberIncl f Y s '' closure ({x'} : Set (g.fiber s)) = C := by
    rw [← hxC.def, ← hρx]
    simpa only [Set.image_singleton] using
      (hclρ.closure_image_eq ({x'} : Set (g.fiber s))).symm
  have hC' : closure ({x'} : Set (g.fiber s)) ∈ irreducibleComponents (g.fiber s) :=
    mem_irreducibleComponents_of_image hclρ.continuous hclρ.injective
      isIrreducible_singleton.closure (by rwa [himg])
  have hdimC : topologicalKrullDim (closure ({x'} : Set (g.fiber s))) =
      topologicalKrullDim C := by
    rw [← himg]
    exact IsHomeomorph.topologicalKrullDim_eq _
      (hclρ.isEmbedding.homeomorphImage (closure ({x'} : Set (g.fiber s)))).isHomeomorph
  have hflat' : AlgebraicGeometry.IsFlatOverAt f.toLRSHom.toShHom F
      (Y.subschemeι (g.fiberι s x')) := by
    rwa [← fiberι_closureFiberIncl, hρx]
  exact hdimC.symm.trans ((topologicalKrullDim_eq_at_generic_component
    (S.residueField s) (g.fiber s) (g.fiberToSpecResidueField s) x'
    (closure ({x'} : Set (g.fiber s))) hC' isGenericPoint_closure).trans
    (topologicalKrullDimAt_fiber_eq_fiber_of_flat f F ξ hξ s x'
      ⟨⟨closure ({x'} : Set (g.fiber s)), hC'⟩, isGenericPoint_closure⟩ hflat'))

/-- A point no other point of whose fibre specializes to it determines a generic point of that
fibre. -/
private theorem mem_genericPoints_asFiber (f : X ⟶ S) (ξ : X)
    (hξ : ∀ w : X, f w = f ξ → w ⤳ ξ → w = ξ) :
    f.asFiber ξ ∈ genericPoints (f.fiber (f ξ)) := by
  rw [mem_genericPoints_iff_forall_specializes_eq]
  intro y hy
  apply (f.fiberι (f ξ)).isEmbedding.injective
  rw [f.fiberι_asFiber ξ]
  refine hξ _ (f.apply_fiberι (f ξ) y) ?_
  simpa only [f.fiberι_asFiber ξ] using hy.map (f.fiberι (f ξ)).continuous

/-- **The fibre dimension along a generalization.** Let `f : X ⟶ S` be locally of finite type and
let `F` be a quasi-coherent `𝒪_X`-module of finite type with support all of `X` which is flat
over `S` at every generic point of every fibre. Let `ξ` be a point of `X` to which no other point
of its own fibre specializes. Then any two irreducible components of fibres, each generated by a
specialization of `ξ`, have the same dimension. -/
@[ega "IV 12.2.1.1" "Dimension comparison"]
theorem topologicalKrullDim_component_fiber_eq_of_specializes (f : X ⟶ S)
    [LocallyOfFiniteType f] (F : X.Modules) [F.IsQuasicoherent] [F.IsFiniteType]
    (hsupp : SheafOfModules.supp F = Set.univ)
    (hflat : ∀ (s : S) (z : f.fiber s), z ∈ genericPoints (f.fiber s) →
      AlgebraicGeometry.IsFlatOverAt f.toLRSHom.toShHom F (f.fiberι s z))
    (ξ : X) (hξ : ∀ w : X, f w = f ξ → w ⤳ ξ → w = ξ)
    (s : S) (x : f.fiber s) (hx : ξ ⤳ f.fiberι s x)
    (C : Set (f.fiber s)) (hC : C ∈ irreducibleComponents (f.fiber s))
    (hxC : IsGenericPoint x C)
    (t : S) (y : f.fiber t) (hy : ξ ⤳ f.fiberι t y)
    (D : Set (f.fiber t)) (hD : D ∈ irreducibleComponents (f.fiber t))
    (hyD : IsGenericPoint y D) :
    topologicalKrullDim C = topologicalKrullDim D := by
  have hass : ξ ∈ Stacks.Divisors.relativeAssassin f F :=
    mem_relativeAssassin_of_mem_genericPoints_fiber f F hsupp ξ
      (mem_genericPoints_asFiber f ξ hξ)
  rw [topologicalKrullDim_component_fiber_eq_closureFiber f F ξ hass s x hx C hC hxC
      (hflat s x (mem_genericPoints_of_isGenericPoint hC hxC)),
    topologicalKrullDim_component_fiber_eq_closureFiber f F ξ hass t y hy D hD hyD
      (hflat t y (mem_genericPoints_of_isGenericPoint hD hyD))]

/-- **Stacks Project, Tag 0GSK, first set of hypotheses.** Let `f : X ⟶ S` be locally of finite
type with `X` integral of generic point `ξ`, and let `F` be a quasi-coherent `𝒪_X`-module of
finite type whose support is all of `X` and which is flat over `S` at every generic point of
every fibre. If the transcendence degree of `κ(ξ)` over `κ(f ξ)` is `d`, then `f` has relative
dimension `d` in the sense of Tag 02NJ.

Only the irreducibility of `X` is used, not its reducedness, and the flatness hypothesis is the
one the source's last sentence allows; flatness of `F` over `S` everywhere, which the source's
list asks for, gives it as `fun s z _ => hF _`. -/
@[stacks 0GSK "first set of hypotheses"]
theorem relativeDimension_of_isGenericPoint_of_trdeg (f : X ⟶ S) [LocallyOfFiniteType f]
    [IsIntegral X] (F : X.Modules) [F.IsQuasicoherent] [F.IsFiniteType]
    (hsupp : SheafOfModules.supp F = Set.univ)
    (hflat : ∀ (s : S) (z : f.fiber s), z ∈ genericPoints (f.fiber s) →
      AlgebraicGeometry.IsFlatOverAt f.toLRSHom.toShHom F (f.fiberι s z))
    (ξ : X) (hξ : IsGenericPoint ξ (Set.univ : Set X)) (d : ℕ)
    (hd : letI := (f.residueFieldMap ξ).hom.toAlgebra
      Cardinal.toENat (Algebra.trdeg (S.residueField (f ξ)) (X.residueField ξ)) = (d : ℕ∞)) :
    AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeDimension f d := by
  let : Algebra ↥(S.residueField (f ξ)) ↥(X.residueField ξ) :=
    (f.residueFieldMap ξ).hom.toAlgebra
  have hd' : Cardinal.toENat
      (Algebra.trdeg (S.residueField (f ξ)) (X.residueField ξ)) = (d : ℕ∞) := hd
  have hfib : IsGenericPoint (f.asFiber ξ) (Set.univ : Set (f.fiber (f ξ))) :=
    isGenericPoint_asFiber f ξ hξ
  have hfibC : (Set.univ : Set (f.fiber (f ξ))) ∈ irreducibleComponents (f.fiber (f ξ)) :=
    ⟨hfib.isIrreducible, fun _ _ _ => Set.subset_univ _⟩
  have hunivdim : topologicalKrullDim (Set.univ : Set (f.fiber (f ξ))) = (d : WithBot ℕ∞) := by
    rw [topologicalKrullDim_eq_at_generic_component
        (S.residueField (f ξ)) (f.fiber (f ξ)) (f.fiberToSpecResidueField (f ξ))
        (f.asFiber ξ) Set.univ hfibC hfib,
      topologicalKrullDimAt_fiber_eq_ringKrullDim_stalk_add_trdeg f ξ,
      ringKrullDim_stalk_eq_zero_of_mem_genericPoints (f.fiber (f ξ)) (f.asFiber ξ)
        (mem_genericPoints_of_isGenericPoint hfibC hfib),
      zero_add, hd']
    rfl
  have hmin : ∀ w : X, f w = f ξ → w ⤳ ξ → w = ξ := fun w _ hw =>
    (hw.antisymm (hξ.specializes (Set.mem_univ w))).eq
  refine relativeDimension_of_forall_component f d fun s C hC => ?_
  let c : f.fiber s := genericPoints.ofComponent ⟨C, hC⟩
  exact (topologicalKrullDim_component_fiber_eq_of_specializes f F hsupp hflat ξ hmin s c
    (hξ.specializes (Set.mem_univ _)) C hC (genericPoints.isGenericPoint_ofComponent ⟨C, hC⟩)
    (f ξ) (f.asFiber ξ)
    (by rw [f.fiberι_asFiber ξ]) Set.univ hfibC hfib).trans hunivdim

/-- The inclusion of a fibre is an affine morphism, being a base change of the morphism from the
spectrum of a residue field, whose source has a single point. -/
private theorem isAffineHom_fiberι (f : X ⟶ S) (s : S) : IsAffineHom (f.fiberι s) := by
  have : IsAffineHom (S.fromSpecResidueField s) :=
    ⟨fun _ _ => IsAffineOpen.of_subsingleton (fun _ _ _ _ => Subsingleton.elim _ _)⟩
  exact MorphismProperty.of_isPullback (P := @IsAffineHom)
    (CategoryTheory.IsPullback.of_hasPullback f (S.fromSpecResidueField s)).flip inferInstance

/-- A point generating an irreducible component of an open subset generates an irreducible
component of the whole space. -/
private theorem closure_mem_irreducibleComponents_of_isOpen {T : Type*} [TopologicalSpace T]
    {V : Set T} (hV : IsOpen V) {p : V} {D : Set V} (hD : D ∈ irreducibleComponents V)
    (hpD : IsGenericPoint p D) :
    closure ({(p : T)} : Set T) ∈ irreducibleComponents T := by
  have hpE : (p : T) ∈ irreducibleComponent (p : T) := mem_irreducibleComponent
  have hirr : IsIrreducible ((Subtype.val : V → T) ⁻¹' irreducibleComponent (p : T)) :=
    isIrreducible_irreducibleComponent.preimage hV.isOpenEmbedding_subtypeVal
      ⟨(p : T), hpE, p, rfl⟩
  have hDsub : D ⊆ (Subtype.val : V → T) ⁻¹' irreducibleComponent (p : T) := by
    rw [← hpD.def]
    exact closure_minimal (Set.singleton_subset_iff.mpr hpE)
      (isClosed_irreducibleComponent.preimage continuous_subtype_val)
  have hpre : (Subtype.val : V → T) ⁻¹' irreducibleComponent (p : T) = D :=
    Set.Subset.antisymm (hD.2 hirr hDsub) hDsub
  have hclosure := closure_image_preimage_of_isPreirreducible (Subtype.val : V → T)
    hV.isOpenMap_subtype_val (irreducibleComponent (p : T)) ⟨p, hpE⟩
    isIrreducible_irreducibleComponent.2 isClosed_irreducibleComponent
  rw [hpre] at hclosure
  have hDimg : closure ((Subtype.val : V → T) '' D) = closure ({(p : T)} : Set T) := by
    rw [← hpD.def, closure_image_closure continuous_subtype_val, Set.image_singleton]
  rw [← hDimg, hclosure]
  exact irreducibleComponent_mem_irreducibleComponents _

/-- If the fibre over `η` is dense in `X`, then every point of `X` is a specialization of a
generic point of an irreducible component of that fibre. Above an affine open of `X` the fibre is
affine, hence a Noetherian space, so it is covered by the closures of finitely many of its
points, and the closure of that finite union is still their union. -/
private theorem exists_mem_genericPoints_specializes (f : X ⟶ S) [LocallyOfFiniteType f]
    (η : S) (hdense : Dense (f ⁻¹' ({η} : Set S))) (x₀ : X) :
    ∃ p : f.fiber η, p ∈ genericPoints (f.fiber η) ∧ f.fiberι η p ⤳ x₀ := by
  have : IsAffineHom (f.fiberι η) := isAffineHom_fiberι f η
  obtain ⟨-, ⟨U, hU, rfl⟩, hx₀U, -⟩ :=
    X.isBasis_affineOpens.exists_subset_of_mem_open (Set.mem_univ x₀) isOpen_univ
  have hVaff : IsAffineOpen ((f.fiberι η) ⁻¹ᵁ U) := hU.preimage (f.fiberι η)
  have : IsNoetherianRing Γ(f.fiber η, (f.fiberι η) ⁻¹ᵁ U) :=
    IsLocallyNoetherian.component_noetherian ⟨_, hVaff⟩
  set V : Set (f.fiber η) := (((f.fiberι η) ⁻¹ᵁ U : (f.fiber η).Opens) : Set (f.fiber η)) with hV
  have hNS : NoetherianSpace V := noetherianSpace_of_isAffineOpen _ hVaff
  have hVopen : IsOpen V := ((f.fiberι η) ⁻¹ᵁ U).isOpen
  have : QuasiSober V := hVopen.isOpenEmbedding_subtypeVal.quasiSober
  have : Finite (irreducibleComponents V) := NoetherianSpace.finite_irreducibleComponents
  set gp : irreducibleComponents V → f.fiber η := fun D => (genericPoints.ofComponent D : _)
  have hupgrade : ∀ D, gp D ∈ genericPoints (f.fiber η) := fun D =>
    closure_mem_irreducibleComponents_of_isOpen hVopen D.2
      (genericPoints.isGenericPoint_ofComponent D)
  have hclosed : IsClosed (⋃ D, closure ({f.fiberι η (gp D)} : Set X)) :=
    isClosed_iUnion_of_finite fun _ => isClosed_closure
  have hsub : (U : Set X) ∩ f ⁻¹' ({η} : Set S) ⊆
      ⋃ D, closure ({f.fiberι η (gp D)} : Set X) := by
    rintro a ⟨ha2, ha1⟩
    obtain ⟨a', rfl⟩ : a ∈ Set.range (f.fiberι η) := by rwa [f.range_fiberι η]
    let v : V := ⟨a', ha2⟩
    let D : irreducibleComponents V :=
      ⟨irreducibleComponent v, irreducibleComponent_mem_irreducibleComponents v⟩
    exact Set.mem_iUnion.mpr ⟨D,
      specializes_iff_mem_closure.mp (((subtype_specializes_iff _ v).mp
      ((genericPoints.isGenericPoint_ofComponent D).specializes
        mem_irreducibleComponent)).map (f.fiberι η).continuous)⟩
  have hcov := (hdense.open_subset_closure_inter U.isOpen).trans (closure_minimal hsub hclosed)
  obtain ⟨D, hD⟩ := Set.mem_iUnion.mp (hcov hx₀U)
  exact ⟨gp D, hupgrade D, specializes_iff_mem_closure.mpr hD⟩

/-- **Stacks Project, Tag 0GSK, second set of hypotheses.** Let `f : X ⟶ S` be locally of finite
type and let `F` be a quasi-coherent `𝒪_X`-module of finite type whose support is all of `X` and
which is flat over `S` at every generic point of every fibre. If the fibre over a point `η` of
`S` is dense in `X` and every irreducible component of that fibre has dimension `d`, then `f` has
relative dimension `d` in the sense of Tag 02NJ.

The source asks in addition that `S` be irreducible with `η` its generic point, which is what
makes the density plausible; the argument uses only the density itself, so that hypothesis is
dropped here and the source's statement is the case of an irreducible `S` and its generic
point. The flatness hypothesis is again the weakened one of the source's last sentence. -/
@[stacks 0GSK "second set of hypotheses"]
theorem relativeDimension_of_dense_fiber_of_component_dim (f : X ⟶ S) [LocallyOfFiniteType f]
    (F : X.Modules) [F.IsQuasicoherent] [F.IsFiniteType]
    (hsupp : SheafOfModules.supp F = Set.univ)
    (hflat : ∀ (s : S) (z : f.fiber s), z ∈ genericPoints (f.fiber s) →
      AlgebraicGeometry.IsFlatOverAt f.toLRSHom.toShHom F (f.fiberι s z))
    (η : S) (hdense : Dense (f ⁻¹' ({η} : Set S))) (d : ℕ)
    (hdim : ∀ Z ∈ irreducibleComponents (f.fiber η), topologicalKrullDim Z = (d : WithBot ℕ∞)) :
    AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeDimension f d := by
  refine relativeDimension_of_forall_component f d fun s C hC => ?_
  let c : f.fiber s := genericPoints.ofComponent ⟨C, hC⟩
  obtain ⟨p, hpgen, hspec⟩ := exists_mem_genericPoints_specializes f η hdense (f.fiberι s c)
  set ξ : X := f.fiberι η p with hξdef
  have hfξ : f ξ = η := f.apply_fiberι η p
  have hmin : ∀ w : X, f w = f ξ → w ⤳ ξ → w = ξ := by
    intro w hw hwξ
    rw [hfξ] at hw
    obtain ⟨w', rfl⟩ : w ∈ Set.range (f.fiberι η) := by rwa [f.range_fiberι η]
    rw [(mem_genericPoints_iff_forall_specializes_eq p).1 hpgen w'
      ((f.fiberι η).isEmbedding.isInducing.specializes_iff.mp hwξ), hξdef]
  have hDcomp : closure ({p} : Set (f.fiber η)) ∈ irreducibleComponents (f.fiber η) := hpgen
  exact (topologicalKrullDim_component_fiber_eq_of_specializes f F hsupp hflat ξ hmin s c
    hspec C hC (genericPoints.isGenericPoint_ofComponent ⟨C, hC⟩) η p specializes_rfl
    (closure ({p} : Set (f.fiber η))) hDcomp isGenericPoint_closure).trans (hdim _ hDcomp)

end Stacks.RelativeAssassin

end
